# Line endings.
#
# Deliberately narrow: only the files the Raspberry Pi actually executes are
# pinned. Everything else is left to each clone's core.autocrlf, so a Windows
# checkout keeps CRLF where CRLF is harmless and no mass renormalisation is
# forced on a working tree.
#
# These types are pinned because CRLF breaks them outright on Linux rather than
# merely looking untidy:
#
#   *.sh        a trailing \r on the shebang gives "bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M"
#   *.py        same, for the server scripts systemd starts
#   *.service   systemd reads the \r as part of the value
#   *.yml       a workflow's `run:` block is handed to a Linux shell verbatim
#   *.conf      nginx config, deployed to the Pi
#   .githooks/  git runs these through sh; they carry no .sh suffix to match
#
# The committed tree is already LF throughout; this keeps it that way when a
# commit is made from a clone that does not normalise, which is how CRLF would
# otherwise reach deploy-pi.yml.

*.sh        text eol=lf
*.py        text eol=lf
*.service   text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
*.conf      text eol=lf
.githooks/* text eol=lf

# Generated files, pinned for the opposite reason: CRLF breaks none of these.
# The tools that write them emit LF, so core.autocrlf expects a CRLF working
# tree it is never given, and git calls them modified forever. That is not only
# noise in every `git status` — git will not overwrite what it believes is an
# edit, so a pull refuses with "local changes would be overwritten" naming files
# nobody has touched.
#
#   arcade/shared/adenosine-*.js and the assets beside them are byte-copied out
#   of the npm packages by scripts/sync-adenosine.mjs
#
# These are safe to pin because npm tarballs are LF whatever any clone's
# autocrlf is set to, so the two ends cannot disagree.
#
# arcade/george-boole/ is deliberately absent, including its tests/. It is not
# authored here: scripts/sync-game.mjs replaces it wholesale with a byte copy of
# web/ from the game's own repo, so the two repos have to want the same endings.
# That repo's .gitattributes declines an eol pin for exactly this reason, and
# pinning this side alone would make every sync land files git reports as
# modified -- the problem these rules exist to remove, on a different schedule.
# Normalising it means changing both repos together, not this one in passing.

arcade/shared/adenosine-*.js             text eol=lf
arcade/shared/chat-worker.js             text eol=lf
arcade/shared/chat-widget.css            text eol=lf
arcade/shared/cards/cards.css            text eol=lf
arcade/shared/chips/chip-animation.css   text eol=lf
arcade/shared/multiplayer/lobby.css      text eol=lf
arcade/puzzle-framework/css/puzzle-*.css text eol=lf
